  "result": "For BOTH generators, the feasible region is EXACTLY level 1 (no cell shape) at ALL FOUR tested symprec values (0.01, 0.05, 0.1, 0.3) -- 4/4 feasible at level 1, 0/4 feasible at levels 2-5, for both MatterGen and CrystalFormer. Symprec, within the tested range, never pushes any level-2-through-5 setting below p=0.5, and never pushes level 1 above p=0.5 either (MatterGen level 1: p ranges 0.152-0.393 across symprec; CrystalFormer level 1: p ranges 0.016-0.047).",
  "feasible_window_survives_2d": "YES. The manuscript's 1-D slice (Table tab:ablation, fixed symprec=0.1) reports level 1 as the only feasible cell-bin setting for both generators. The full 2-D grid confirms this is not an artifact of the particular symprec chosen for that table: the same level-1-only feasible region holds at every symprec value tested (0.01-0.3). The design recommendation (drop cell shape; keep composition+orbit information only) is validated across the full tested tolerance range, not just at the single symprec value the manuscript happened to tabulate.",
  "correction_to_design_recommendation": "None needed. This is a confirmation, not a correction: no narrower true window was hiding in the untested symprec dimension, and no wider apparent window at symprec=0.1 fails to generalize to other symprec values.",
  "caveat": "The joint grid covers only the two generators with paired raw/DFT-relaxed sets (MatterGen, CrystalFormer). WyLLM-vanilla-DiffCSP++ has no paired relaxed set in this corpus, so its stability side of the trade-off (and therefore any 2-D feasibility statement for it) remains unmeasurable, exactly as already documented in fingerprint_ablation_results.json and the manuscript's table note.",
  "analysis": "joint_granularity: joint symprec x cell_bin grid, feasible-window-in-2D check"
